<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Dry weather continues.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Dry weather continues.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dry, cool weather conditions continued to hover over the U.S. northern Plains Thursday, allowing farmers to catch up on fieldwork, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Movement of grain remained slack as producers focused on getting their crops planted.</p>
<p>&quot;One guy let go 6,000 bushels of wheat today, but other than that it's very quiet here and (producers) are still seeding away,&quot; a Montana dealer said.</p>
<p>Basis levels for dark northern spring wheat were mostly flat, dealers said.  </p>
